{"name":"Enchantress","hex":"#5d3a47","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"enchantress","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woman, especially an attractive one, skilled at using magic; an alluring witch.","A beautiful, charming and irresistible woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enchantress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Incantation","blocks":[{"text":"An incantation, spell, charm, enchantment, or bewitchery is a magical formula intended to trigger a magical effect on a person or objects. The formula can be spoken, sung, or chanted. An incantation can also be performed during ceremonial rituals or prayers. In the world of magic, wizards, witches, and fairies are common performers of incantations in culture and folklore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Book_of_incantations_f.7v.png/330px-Book_of_incantations_f.7v.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incantation","wikidata":"Q1999796"},{"title":"Magician (fantasy)","blocks":[{"text":"A magician, also known as a mage, magus, magic-user, spellcaster, enchanter/enchantress, sorcerer/sorceress, warlock, witch, or wizard, is someone who uses or practices magic derived from supernatural, occult, or arcane sources. Magicians enjoy a rich history in mythology, legends, fiction, and folklore, and are common figures in works of fantasy, such as fantasy literature and role-playing games."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg/330px-The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magician_(fantasy)","wikidata":"Q148401"},{"title":"Enchantress (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Enchantress is the common primary alias of two fictional characters appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The first of these is a powerful sorceress by the name of Amora, depicted as one of Thor's greatest enemies. The second Enchantress is Sylvie Lushton, who was given great mystic powers by Loki when he created her as a tool for chaos. She models herself after the original Enchantress, Amora."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Enchantress_%28Marvel_Comics%29_art_by_Jo_Chen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enchantress_(Marvel_Comics)","wikidata":"Q587036"},{"title":"Enchantress (DC Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"The Enchantress is a supervillain appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics. Created by Bob Haney and Howard Purcell, the character made her first appearance in Strange Adventures #187."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/Enchantress_DC_Comics.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enchantress_(DC_Comics)","wikidata":"Q5375407"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0d/Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Classic magic words","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbracadabra_triangle_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Orlando_Furioso_13.jpg/500px-Orlando_Furioso